            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The house airtightness if fairly low. We recommend to verify and replace the weatherstrips of the windows and doors. Also, we suggest adding weather stripping on the edge of the attic hatch. It might reduce the heat loss from the attic.</airSeal>
                <AdditionalComments>The depressurization test result indicates that there is a risk of a backdraft of the combustion gases to come back into the living space. This represents the danger of CO2 poisoning. The installation of a Carbon Monoxide detector is strongly recommended.</AdditionalComments>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
